"""fig3c_metric_provenance_check.csv | main Fig. 3 (04_figures/fig.3/fig3_main_A4_v2.py)

Recovered statistical-analysis script | reproducibility package | Fig. 3 track.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code cross checks whether pairwise similarity between simulated
    functional connectivity models (10m, 100m, and 1b voxel population
    sizes) is consistent depending on which data source and which subject
    subset are used. For each pair of models it computes Pearson
    correlations across edges for each subject, then summarizes those per
    subject correlations into a mean using both a plain average and a
    Fisher z transformed average, comparing results computed from the new
    mat file simulation arrays against results computed from an archived
    wide format CSV of the same simulated edges, and comparing the full 12
    subject set against the 9 subject subset with complete archive data.
    One row of the output table represents one specific combination of a
    model pair, a data source, and a subject subset, reporting the number
    of subjects used, the two averaged correlation values computed from
    that combination, and the corresponding similarity value originally
    reported in the fc_similarity_six_models_new3m reference for that same
    model pair.

INPUT FILES
    archive simulation_results_wide_12subs.csv
    {B}/revision/10m_voxel_population_simulation/simulate_FC_edges.csv
    {B}/revision/model_scale_consistent/simulation_results_wide_12subs.csv
    {VX}/new10m_simulated_FC_12subs_with_empirical.mat

OUTPUT FILE
    fig3c_metric_provenance_check.csv
    written to OUT_DIR (default /tmp/recovery_scratch/fig3)
    reference copy in this package: 04_figures/fig.3/fig3_data/fig3c_metric_provenance_check.csv

STATISTICAL TESTS
    Pearson correlation
    Fisher z transform

RUNNABLE ON A LAPTOP
    conditional on the input files above being present on this machine

SEED
    not applicable (deterministic computation)

PROVENANCE
    execution-log cell : e42961c2-2a6a-4710-b411-85df8fbcc0bd
    frame              : fe47a03f-2d43-4fe0-a1c3-e0544839d822
    ran                : 2026-09-22 17:10:37 UTC
    conda environment  : python
    verbatim archive   : recovered/fig3/fig3c_metric_provenance_check__cell_e42961c2.py
    candidates found   : 1

REORGANISATION APPLIED
    A header was added; the imports, the input paths and the constants the
    interactive cell inherited from earlier cells in its session were made
    explicit; exploratory prints and abandoned branches were dropped; all file
    writes were redirected to OUT_DIR.  No computation, test, covariate,
    correction or seed was changed.
"""

